{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795650152,"nonce":"JK45duFsxQj+tybUFwfIGZerSr8=","title":"CSS reload test fails when a save is read half way","message":"`bursts_coalesce_and_unrelated_files_do_not_trigger_reloads` failed on the Linux CI runner: after the first wake the source was \"\" and not the last saved rule.\n\nThe test writes the watched file ten times and takes one reload to carry the last text. `std::fs::write` empties the file and then writes it. If the writer is held for longer than the watcher's settle time between the two, the watcher reads the empty file, which is a valid sheet, wakes the app, and wakes it again for the real text.\n\nReproduced by creating the file, sleeping 300 ms and writing it: the old test fails with the same message.\n\nFix: the test reloads until the last text arrives, then drains further wakes, before it checks that saving the same text again does not wake the app. The watcher is unchanged. The other reload tests save once and have the same window, which is much narrower there.","files":null}]}